# width: 120
# // changed (railmove): the launcher dock lists every INSTALLED, not
# disabled integration whatever its chip flags say. Claude Code, Codex
# and HTTP ship with their chip hidden — the `(hidden)` the Installed
# tab paints, which is the tab cluster's question — and the strip used
# to read that flag as "not enabled", so none of the three was ever on
# the dock. "Hide the chip" and "not on the dock" are two wishes.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex dock always
ex dock start
expect screen contains "Browser"
expect screen contains "Claude Code"
expect screen contains "Codex"
expect screen contains "HTTP"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# The chips are exactly as hidden as they were: the Installed tab
# still says so (the column clips the badge; a drag reads the row).
command view.activity_integrations
expect screen contains "Inst (4)"
drag 30 5 70 5
expect screen contains "Claude Code (hidden)  first-party"
expect screen contains "Codex (hidden)  first-party"
expect screen contains "HTTP (hidden)  first-party"
# Still on the strip, in the same breath.
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen contains "Codex"
